.TH TENSQUANT 1 "31 October 2026" "tenskit 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tensquant \- dequantize a pack, or quantize with Q4_0 or Q8_0
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY tensquant
.B \-\-dequant
.B \-o
.I out
.RB [ \-\-format
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.RB [ \-\-force\-single\-file ]
.I source
.YS
.SY tensquant
.B \-\-quantize
.I q4_0|q8_0
.B \-o
.I out.gguf
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.RB [ \-\-force\-single\-file ]
.I source
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tensquant
reads a container and writes float32, or the reverse for the two
reference quantizers.
Dequant does not recover the original pre-quant floats.
A directory is the safetensors weight set, the same rule as
.BR \%tenspile (1).
An existing output file is left in place unless
.B \-\-force
is set.
.PP
.B \-\-dequant
writes quantized and float tensors as float32, shaped
.IR "[out_features, in_features]" ,
and copies integer and bool tensors unchanged.
GGML blocks use the transcribed dequantize formulas.
Q8_1 is refused.
GPTQ uses the 2, 4, and 8 bit cuda pack, which is also the stored
exllama layout.
Zeros are incremented before the scale for
.IR checkpoint_format " gptq"
and used as stored for
.IR gptq_v2 ,
and
.I g_idx
selects the row.
AWQ uses the gemm nibble order.
bitsandbytes uses the NF4 or FP4 codebook.
compressed-tensors takes each module's scheme from
.I \%config_groups
in file order, expands preset names, and applies the scale and zero point
to pack-quantized or naive-quantized codes.
MLX uses
.I \%quantization
in
.IR config.json ,
and infers the mode of a module with no entry, using the input width from
.I config.json
for LLaMA modules.
.PP
GPTQ 3-bit, the marlin tile inverse, EXL2
.RI ( EXL2\-Q1 ),
and ModelOpt NVFP4
.RI ( CT\-Q1 )
stop, because those inverses are not written out.
.PP
.B \-\-quantize
accepts
.I q4_0
and
.I q8_0
and writes a GGUF file with those reference quantizers.
K-quants and IQ types are not quantized.
A matrix whose innermost size is not a multiple of 32 is written F16.
.SH OPTIONS
Pass
.B \-\-dequant
or
.BR \-\-quantize ,
not both.
.TP
.B \-\-dequant
Write float32 from a transcribed pack.
.TP
.BI \-\-quantize " q4_0|q8_0"
Quantize float weights with the named reference quantizer.
The output is GGUF.
Matrices are quantized.
Tensors of rank 1 or below, names ending in
.IR _norm.weight ,
names that do not end in
.IR .weight ,
.IR .lora_a ,
or
.IR .lora_b ,
and roles such as
.I ffn_gate_inp
stay F32.
Names that are not GGUF names are first resolved to their GGUF role through
.I config.json
.IR architectures[0] ;
a name with no role is F32 only for rank 1 or a name not ending in
.IR .weight ,
and a warning lists it.
The per-architecture
.I tensor_force_quant
overrides are not applied.
Integer tensors are copied.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIfile\fR"
Output path.
Required.
For
.BR \-\-dequant ,
the container is safetensors, npy, or npz,
from
.B \-\-format
or from the file name.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " name"
Container to write for
.BR \-\-dequant .
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite an existing output file.
.TP
.BI \-\-force\-single\-file " path"
Read this
.I .safetensors
file even when
.I config.json
is in the same directory.
It applies only to the path written immediately after it.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the short help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The output file was written.
.TP
.B 1
An error.
The message is written to stderr and starts with
.BR "\%tensquant: " .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Dequantize a GGUF file to float32 safetensors:
.RS
.EX
tensquant \-\-dequant \-o model\-f32.safetensors model.gguf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Dequantize a GPTQ, AWQ, compressed-tensors, or MLX model; pass the directory so config.json is read:
.RS
.EX
tensquant \-\-dequant \-o model\-f32.safetensors model/
.EE
.RE
.PP
Dequantize into one .npz archive:
.RS
.EX
tensquant \-\-dequant \-o weights.npz model/
.EE
.RE
.PP
Quantize a model to Q8_0 GGUF:
.RS
.EX
tensquant \-\-quantize q8_0 \-o model\-q8.gguf model/
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config.json
Beside the source file or in the source directory.
.B \-\-dequant
reads
.I \%quantization_config
(GPTQ, AWQ, bitsandbytes, compressed-tensors) or
.I quantization
(MLX) from it, and
.B \-\-quantize
reads
.I \%architectures[0]
to resolve tensor roles.
.TP
.I .OUTPUT.tensquant\-spill
Beside the output.
.B \-\-dequant
writes each float32 tensor here as soon as it is computed,
so memory holds about one tensor rather than the whole model.
The file is as large as the output and is removed when tensquant exits.
.SH AUTHOR
Nick Reynolds (GitHub and X: goldnode).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR \%tenspile (1),
.BR \%tensinfo (1),
.BR \%tensdiff (1),
.BR \%tensconv (1)
